        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0116" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg54"/>

                <head>No. 44.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilson to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7, 1878</date>.
                        (Received April 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I hasten to inform you that, in accordance
                    with instructions contained in your dispatch dated the 14th March, and received
                    at this legation yesterday morning, I sent immediately to the minister for
                    foreign affairs a communication, the copy of which is herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I hope to see him personally to-day, and shall then read to him the text of the
                    act of Congress inclosed in your dispatch, and explain to him more fully the
                    necessity of an early reply.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. WILSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d49-a1.xml" xpointer="d49-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
